fmt writes through os.Stdout, which is a nil @File on bare-metal by design (os_baremetal.bn: "a bare-metal target has no standard output" — its Write returns errNoFS), so fmt produces no output there and the expected text is unattainable. This is an environment limitation, not a codegen bug: fmt.Sprint (bypasses os.Stdout) formats every operand correctly on native arm32, and the println builtin prints via semihosting. Hosted/VM-only test. Covers BOTH baremetal lanes: builder-comp_arm32_baremetal (this marker, LLVM) and builder-comp_native_arm32_baremetal (via OVERRIDE_MODE, run.sh).
